# Error Handling

## Central handler

All API errors go through `GlobalExceptionHandler` + `ApiResponseBuilder`. Controllers do not catch exceptions for HTTP responses.

| Exception | HTTP | Log level |
|-----------|------|-----------|
| `ResourceNotFoundException` | 404 | WARN |
| `IllegalArgumentException` | 400 | WARN |
| `MethodArgumentNotValidException` | 400 | DEBUG |
| `Exception` (catch-all) | 500 | ERROR (stack trace) |

## Envelope shapes

**Standard error:** `timestamp`, `status`, `error`, `message`

**Validation error:** `timestamp`, `status`, `error` (`Validation failed`), `details` (field → message map)

**Delete success:** `ApiResponseBuilder.messagePayload("… deleted successfully", "id", id)`

## Rules

- Never expose raw `ex.getMessage()` on 500 — return `"An unexpected error occurred"`
- Use `ResourceNotFoundException(error, message)` or `forResourceWithId(resource, id)`
- Register new domain exceptions in `GlobalExceptionHandler` before the catch-all `Exception` handler

```java
// GOOD
log.error("Unexpected error", ex);
return ApiResponseBuilder.error(INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, "Unexpected error", UNEXPECTED_ERROR_MESSAGE);

// BAD
return ApiResponseBuilder.error(INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, "Unexpected error", ex.getMessage());
```
